-- Uruguay deep-dive content (English). Uruguay's CFE (Comprobante Fiscal
-- Electrónico) system, run by DGI, is one of the oldest mandatory
-- e-invoicing regimes in Latin America -- but its technical model is
-- genuinely distinct from the region's newer real-time clearance
-- systems (Mexico's CFDI, Chile's DTE): DGI pre-authorizes blocks of
-- sequential invoice numbers (CAE) rather than approving each document
-- individually before it reaches the buyer, so this page deliberately
-- avoids describing it as flat "real-time clearance." Live-researched
-- against DGI's own site (efactura.dgi.gub.uy, gub.uy), IMPO (Uruguay's
-- official legal gazette/database), the CIAT country profile, and
-- industry tax-technology advisories. Penalties are framed qualitatively
-- per Decreto 36/012 Art. 17's own cross-reference to the general
-- Código Tributario regime -- no CFE-specific fine schedule exists, and
-- an unsourced peso range found circulating in vendor content could not
-- be independently verified, so it's deliberately not repeated here.









